<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 62,580 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 62,580 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 62,580 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 70,346 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			11,380	    10,287</p>
<p>    Import cargo			51,200	    60,059</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and 12 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		66,000	 Johar		   1/6</p>
<p>Gas oil		  60,000	 CSP - 10		2/7</p>
<p>Palm oil		  4,000	 Freja Nordic	 29/6</p>
<p>High speed diesel    28,313	 Apsheron	     28/6</p>
<p>Vegoil		   10,080	 Cielo Di-Milano    28/6</p>
<p>Gas oil		  60,000	 Themera		 due</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 24,510	 Addax		   due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
